abstract: >-
  A weighted, progressive certification framework for Foundational Data
  Products. Eight dimensions (Data Quality, Semantic Coherence, Metadata
  Completeness, Lineage Transparency, Security and Compliance, Governance,
  Performance, Accessibility and Interoperability) are assessed through
  twenty-four criteria scored from 0 to 100 and combined into a
  certification percentage. Certification levels (Registered, Bronze,
  Silver, Gold) combine the percentage with tier checks, dimension floors,
  three-owner sign-off and a portability condition. The dimension profile
  travels with the product in its passport, so each consumer, including
  AI agents, can judge fitness for its own purpose. Part of the Foundeon
  methodology.
